# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) for local dev. Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_.

# Data source toggle. "mock" (default) runs the app entirely off the in-memory fake data layer
# (src/api/mock.ts) — no backend, no auth, fully demoable. "live" hits the contract API.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=mock

# API base for VITE_DATA_SOURCE=live. In production the deployed build reads this from a runtime
# /config.json (written by CDK), so this is only a dev override.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://<api-id>.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com

# Cognito Hosted-UI + PKCE sign-in for the dashboard API (see src/auth/cognito.ts). Auth engages
# ONLY when BOTH the domain and client id are set — leave them unset for local dev / mock so the
# app stays login-free. In production these are written into the runtime /config.json at deploy
# time. VITE_REDIRECT_URI is optional and defaults to `${window.location.origin}/`.
# VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=https://your-portal.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com
# VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=your-app-client-id
# VITE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/
